# Modern code standards

When writing or refactoring code, use latest stable language features and built-ins. Avoid legacy patterns and polyfills for native features.

## TypeScript & JavaScript (NestJS services)

- Prefer `import type` for type-only imports.
- Prefer `satisfies` over widening `as` when validating structure.
- Avoid `enum` unless required; prefer as-const objects or union types.
- Use `?.`, `??`, `??=` / `&&=` / `||=`, and `Object.hasOwn()`.
- Prefer native `async/await` over callback or deep `.then` chains.

## Python 3.11+ (vision-engine)

- Built-in generics: `list[str]`, `dict[str, int]` — not `typing.List` / `Dict`.
- Unions: `str | None` — not `Optional[str]` / `Union[...]`.
- Prefer `match` / `case` for complex branching.
- Prefer FastAPI / Pydantic v2 patterns (`model_config`, `Annotated`) over legacy v1 APIs.
- Keep NumPy/OpenCV arrays typed clearly at service boundaries (bytes in, structured results out).
